### Design Rationale

| Decision | Justification |
|----------|---------------|
| Rule type: `position_near_with_facing` | Per guidelines, this is the PREFERRED rule for find/locate/observe tasks. It correctly models "player can see the target." |
| `max_distance: 5.0` | Spawn is ~11.3 blocks from target, so 5.0 ensures the player has intentionally navigated toward the pillar. Not too tight (player doesn't need to touch it) but ensures real movement. |
| `facing_tolerance: 60` | Standard tolerance for find tasks. Ensures the player is looking in the general direction of the chiseled sandstone, confirming visual identification. |
| `target: [8, 1, 8]` | The lower chiseled sandstone block, which is at player eye-level when standing on the sand floor (Y=0 for feet, Y≈1.6 for eyes). This is the most natural block to look at when approaching. |
| Single rule (not multiple) | One `position_near_with_facing` rule captures both proximity AND facing in a single check, which is cleaner and matches the evaluator's supported rule types exactly. |

